# Keep docs and Hesk current (PC2)

A behavior or ops change is unfinished until the matching docs match the code in the **same turn**.

## What to update

| Audience | Where | When |
|----------|--------|------|
| **Owner / product law** | `docs/business-rules.md` | Any rule cashiers or owners must know (sign-in, money, refuse lists, screens) |
| **Technical / operators** | `docs/http-edge.md`, `README.md` Load/Application, and other `docs/*.md` that name the path | Bootstrap, deploy, env, CLI, proofs, HTTP edge |
| **Hesk (readable map)** | Matching `docs/hesk-kb/*.md` seed | Same facts as above, in the article template |

`docs/business-rules.md` and `docs/PLAN.md` win on conflicts. Hesk mirrors them; it does not invent law.

## Done bar

1. Edit or confirm the owner sentence in `business-rules.md` when product behavior changed.
2. Edit or confirm the technical note (`http-edge.md`, README, PLAN) when operators or agents need a different command or path.
3. Edit the matching Hesk seed (`as_of`, body, Source). Set `hesk: pending` until published.
4. When Hesk is reachable on this machine, run `php docs/hesk-kb/publish-to-hesk.php` and leave seeds `hesk: published YYYY-MM-DD`.
5. Do not ship “not in PC2 product code yet” Hesk text for behavior that is already live, or the reverse.

```text
BAD: lockout changed in EmailSignIn.php; E10 and business-rules still say email+address
GOOD: code, business-rules, http-edge/README if needed, and hesk-kb seed updated together; publish when Hesk is up
```
